        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur White, David Jason, John Sullivan, Derek Trotter, Denzil Tulser, Ernie Trigg\n- Works: A Touch of Frost, Only Fools and Horses\n- Roles: police archivist\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur White was born in 1933 and is an English stage and screen actor.\n- Arthur White is best known for his occasional role as police archivist Ernie Trigg in the crime drama \"A Touch of Frost\".\n- Arthur White appeared in \"A Touch of Frost\" alongside his real-life younger brother, David Jason.\n- David Jason is best known for portraying Derek Trotter in the British television series \"Only Fools and Horses\".\n- Derek Trotter was known by the nickname Del Boy in \"Only Fools and Horses\".\n- John Sullivan wrote the British television series \"Only Fools and Horses\".\n- In \"Only Fools and Horses\", Denzil Tulser is a good friend of Del Boy.",
