        "original_id": "e81ebf9e-c88d-55d9-a295-2a9fd4e5baab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Jason, Arthur White, John Sullivan\n- TV series: Only Fools and Horses, A Touch of Frost\n- Fictional characters: Derek \"Del Boy\" Trotter, Jack Frost, Ernie Trigg, Denzil Tulser\n\nFacts:\n- Only Fools and Horses is a British television sitcom created and written by John Sullivan.\n- Arthur White, born in 1933, is an English stage and screen actor.\n- David Jason is best known for portraying Derek \"Del Boy\" Trotter in the BBC comedy series Only Fools and Horses.\n- David Jason is also best known for portraying Detective Inspector Jack Frost in the ITV crime drama A Touch of Frost.\n- Arthur White is best known for his occasional role as police archivist Ernie Trigg in A Touch of Frost.\n- Arthur White is the real-life older brother of David Jason.\n- Denzil Tulser is a long-distance lorry driver originally from Liverpool.\n- Denzil Tulser is a good friend of Derek Trotter and is one of Del's victims in dodgy goods dealings.",
